msgid "Npc_Ronald"
msgstr "Ronald the Smith"

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Greeting_1"
msgstr "Mind the sparks. You need steel, or you need talking to? Either way, say it plain."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_Trade"
msgstr "What metal have you got?"

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_AskForge"
msgstr "You were not always a smith."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_AboutForge_1"
msgstr "No. I carried a spear before I carried a hammer. The forge feeds the village; the spear only fed the crows."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Farewell_1"
msgstr "Go on, then. Keep your edge oiled and your back to a wall."

# ------------------------------
# Trials of the Strong (Ronald)
# ------------------------------

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Fang"
msgstr "Trial of the Fang"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Fang_Description"
msgstr "Ronald has set out the first of his trials. A wolf waits on the flat ground past the forge — the smallest thing he could find that still bites back. Put it down and come back to him."

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Fang_Stage_Hunt"
msgstr "Put the wolf down"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Fang_Obj_Kill"
msgstr "Kill the wolf on the trial ground"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Pack"
msgstr "Trial of the Pack"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Pack_Description"
msgstr "The second trial. A direwolf — bigger than the last one, quicker than it looks, and it hunts thinking. Ronald wants to see whether you can finish what you start."

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Pack_Stage_Hunt"
msgstr "Put the direwolf down"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Pack_Obj_Kill"
msgstr "Kill the direwolf on the trial ground"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Mountain"
msgstr "Trial of the Mountain"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Mountain_Description"
msgstr "The third trial. A bear: slow, enormous, and it takes a great deal of killing. Ronald says there is no clever way past it — only through."

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Mountain_Stage_Hunt"
msgstr "Put the bear down"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Mountain_Obj_Kill"
msgstr "Kill the bear on the trial ground"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Grave"
msgstr "Trial of the Grave"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Grave_Description"
msgstr "The fourth trial. Ronald has arranged something the graves gave back — old, patient, and far past anything the forest sends. He calls it the last lesson he has to give."

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Grave_Stage_Hunt"
msgstr "Put the revenant down"

msgid "Quest_Trial_Of_The_Grave_Obj_Kill"
msgstr "Kill the grave revenant on the trial ground"

msgid "Ornament_Tier_1"
msgstr "Lesser Ornament"

msgid "Ornament_Tier_1_Description"
msgstr "Grants an ability one more tier 1 socket. An ability wears one ornament at a time; move it freely."

msgid "Ornament_Tier_2"
msgstr "Greater Ornament"

msgid "Ornament_Tier_2_Description"
msgstr "Grants an ability one more tier 2 socket. An ability wears one ornament at a time; move it freely."

msgid "Ornament_Tier_3"
msgstr "Sovereign Ornament"

msgid "Ornament_Tier_3_Description"
msgstr "Grants an ability one more tier 3 socket. An ability wears one ornament at a time; move it freely."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_Trials"
msgstr "I want a real test. Have you got one?"

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Trials_1"
msgstr "Trials, then. I keep a patch of flat ground past the forge, and I put something worth beating on it. Beat it, and I will show you what I saw while you fought. That is the whole arrangement."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_Trial_Fang"
msgstr "Start me small. What is first?"

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_Trial_Pack"
msgstr "I am ready for the second."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_Trial_Mountain"
msgstr "Give me the third."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_Trial_Grave"
msgstr "Whatever is left. Set it loose."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialAccepted_1"
msgstr "It is waiting past the forge, out where the fence gives up. Take your time walking. Take none once you are there."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialWatch_1"
msgstr "Still on my side of the fence, I see. The ground has not moved."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_TrialHint"
msgstr "Remind me what I am walking into."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialHint_Fang_1"
msgstr "A wolf, and not a big one. Past the forge, out where the fence gives up and the trees start. Mind its footing, not its teeth."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialHint_Pack_1"
msgstr "A direwolf. Bigger than the last, and it picks its moment instead of just charging. Same ground past the forge. Do not let it pick the moment for you."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialHint_Mountain_1"
msgstr "A bear. It will not dodge and there is a great deal of it to get through. Same ground past the forge. Go through it, or do not go at all."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialHint_Grave_1"
msgstr "Something the graves gave back — older than this village and in no hurry at all. Past the forge, same as always. It thinks, so do not give it time to."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialReport_1"
msgstr "You walked back. That is already more than some manage. Say it."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_Opt_TrialTurnIn"
msgstr "It is done."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialPraise_1"
msgstr "Good. You held ground where I would have expected you to give it. Breathe, then come find me — there is a harder one waiting."

msgid "Dlg_Ronald_TrialPraiseLast_1"
msgstr "Done, and done well. That is the end of what I can set in front of you. Whatever comes next, you will be the one choosing it."


